      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Open viewing with Stuart McDonnell\r\nSaturday 3rd October | 11–11:15 a.m.\r\n\r\nJoin me this Saturday for a look around. I’ll be on hand to show you through and answer any questions. See you there!\r\n\r\n\r\nStuart McDonnell Properties are delighted to present No. 18 Strand Road to the market, a charming original Coast Guard cottage in one of Baldoyle’s most special coastal settings.\r\nThere is something instantly appealing about this little stretch of Strand Road. Step outside your front door and Baldoyle Bay is right there in front of you, while from the house itself there are wonderful, uninterrupted views across the estuary towards Sutton and Portmarnock Golf Clubs and out towards Ireland’s Eye.\r\nIt is a view that is never really the same twice. The tide comes and goes, the light changes throughout the day and the bay is constantly alive with birdlife. Baldoyle Bay is both a Special Area of Conservation and a Special Protection Area, making this a very special place to call home.\r\nTo the front, a cobbled driveway provides ample off-street parking for multiple cars, a particularly useful feature in such a lovely coastal setting.\r\nThe cottage itself has plenty of personality. The entrance porch opens through to a comfortable living room with a feature gas fireplace, recessed lighting and an open staircase, all adding to the relaxed character you would hope to find in a period coastal home.\r\nTo the rear is the kitchen and dining area, fitted with wall and floor units, stone worktops and integrated appliances, with plenty of room to sit around the table and enjoy everyday life.\r\nUpstairs there are two bedrooms and the bathroom. The front bedroom is particularly lovely, with two windows looking straight across the bay, not a bad view to wake up to every morning. It also has fitted wardrobes, recessed lighting and access to the attic, which may offer further possibilities subject to feasibility and any necessary planning permission.\r\nThe Sunny Southwest-facing rear garden is another real plus, with a patio area to catch the afternoon and evening sun, two sheds and pedestrian access onto the rear laneway. No. 18 also comes with a separate piece of land to the rear, an unusual and interesting addition to the property presenting multiple opportunities.\r\nThe house has been well cared for over the years and retains plenty of character, with double-glazed windows, gas-fired central heating and a gas boiler replaced within the last three years. It also gives the next owner the opportunity to put their own stamp on it over time.\r\nAnd then there is Baldoyle itself.\r\nYou can leave the house and be walking along the coast in minutes, continue along the greenway towards Portmarnock or head in the other direction towards Sutton and Howth. Baldoyle village is close by for everyday amenities, while Sutton DART Station provides an easy connection into the city. Despite all of that convenience, Strand Road still has that lovely feeling of being tucked away beside the water.\r\nNo. 18 isn't a conventional two-bedroom house, and that is very much part of its charm. An original Coast Guard cottage, generous off-street parking, a southwest-facing garden, a separate piece of land and those wonderful views across Baldoyle Bay combine to make this a home with a real sense of place.\r\nContact Stuart McDonnell Properties to arrange your viewing. Let’s get you moving."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance porch — 2.57m × 1.94m\r\nFront entrance porch with sliding door to the living room.\r\nLiving room — 4.97m × 3.13m\r\nFeature gas fireplace, recessed lighting, sliding door to the entrance porch and open staircase leading to the first-floor landing.\r\nKitchen/dining room — 4.95m × 2.82m\r\nFitted wall and floor units with stone countertop, integrated oven, integrated hob, extractor fan and integrated fridge freezer. Plumbed for a dishwasher. Recessed lighting, tiled kitchen flooring and wood flooring in the dining area.\r\nLanding\r\nAccessed by the open staircase.\r\nBathroom — 2.47m at longest × 1.56m\r\nJacuzzi bath with electric shower, WC, wash hand basin and hot press.\r\nBedroom 1 — 3.24m × 3.10m at widest\r\nFront bedroom with fitted wardrobes, recessed lighting and attic access. Two windows enjoy views across Baldoyle Estuary towards Sutton Golf Club and Portmarnock Golf Club.\r\nBedroom 2 — 3.13m × 2.31m\r\nRear garden — 7.53m × 5.39m\r\nSouthwest-facing garden with patio area, barn shed, concrete shed and a door to the rear laneway.\r\nAdditional land\r\nSeparate piece of land to the rear of the property, with opportunities for multiple uses."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tOriginal Coast Guard cottage.\r\n•\tSeparate piece of land to the rear with multiple opportunities.\r\n•\tSunny Southwest-facing rear garden with patio area.\r\n•\tBeautiful views across Baldoyle Estuary towards Sutton and Portmarnock golf clubs.\r\n•\tCobbled driveway with off street parking for multiple cars. \r\n•\tTwo-bedroom accommodation.\r\n•\tOpen-plan living with an open staircase.\r\n•\tRecessed lighting.\r\n•\tFitted kitchen with stone countertop and integrated appliances.\r\n•\tDoor to rear laneway.\r\n•\tBarn shed and concrete shed.\r\n•\tGas-fired central heating.\r\n•\tBoiler replaced within the last three years.\r\n•\tDouble-glazed windows.\r\n•\tEntrance porch.\r\n•\tAttic conversion possibilities, subject to feasibility and any necessary planning permission.\r\n•\tBER rating: E2\r\n•\tBER number: 114416969\r\n•\tEircode: D13H6V2\r\n•\tArea: c.65.49sqm/704sq.ft\r\n•\tYear of construction c.1890.\r\nLocation\r\nBaldoyle’s coastal setting is a large part of its appeal, combining the character of a former fishing village with local shopping, parks and coastal walks. Seagrange Park adds playgrounds and sports pitches to the area’s outdoor amenities. Fingal County Council — Baldoyle\r\nThe Baldoyle–Portmarnock greenway is another highlight, providing a 1.8km walking and cycling route through Racecourse Park, alongside the Coast Road. With coastal views along the route, it offers an attractive setting for a walk or cycle. \r\nSutton DART station provides a public transport option for travel towards Dublin city centre and Howth, complementing the area’s coastal lifestyle. Iarnród Éireann — Sutton station\r\nContact Stuart McDonnell Properties to arrange your viewing. Let’s get you moving."
